## PR Title
Fix testcases for sb, sh

## PR Description
"change the WE in MA from 1 bit to 4 bits to support byte level write; change the WE of FSM accordingly; fix sb and sh (fix WD)"

This is the follow-up to PR #80 (which fixed `lb`/`lh`/`lhu`). The Memory-Access Write Enable signal is widened from 1 bit to 4 bits to support byte-granularity writes; the FSM is updated accordingly; the `sb` and `sh` store instructions are corrected (including the write-data path). The MemoryLoader module is also enhanced to prepare data for storing into memory, where dataB is the raw word from the CPU and `__tmp_MemData` together with `MemWriteByteAddress` selects which byte to write.

